# ammonia.allowlist (sample)
#
# Install as: /private/var/ammonia/core/ammonia.allowlist
#
# PRESENCE of this file switches ammonia into strict default-deny mode:
# libopener (the component that loads and runs tweaks) is injected ONLY into
# executables listed below. Every other process — GUI apps and headless
# daemons alike — runs untouched. Remove the file to return to the default
# role-based behaviour (all GUI-role apps unless ammonia.blacklist excludes
# them).
#
# Notes:
#   - One entry per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#     Inline comments are NOT supported — a '#' after an entry becomes part of
#     the entry. Put comments on their own line.
#   - Matching is on the WHOLE executable name: either the full path, or the
#     final path component (basename). "Safari" matches
#     /Applications/Safari.app/Contents/MacOS/Safari but not "SafariServices".
#   - An empty/all-comment file means deny everything (nothing is injected).
#   - The lightweight spawn hook (liblibinfect) still loads into launchd and
#     xpcproxy regardless; it runs no tweak code. Only libopener is gated here.
#   - If you rely on the logout fix, you MUST list loginwindow explicitly:
#       /System/Library/CoreServices/loginwindow.app/Contents/MacOS/loginwindow
#
# Examples (delete and replace with your own):
# /System/Library/CoreServices/loginwindow.app/Contents/MacOS/loginwindow
# Finder
# Safari
